<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roosevelt Skerrit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roosevelt Skerrit is a Dominican politician of the Dominica Labour Party who became prime minister in 2004, at 31 one of the youngest heads of government in the world. His long tenure has seen recovery from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-maria">Hurricane Maria</a> in 2017 and heavy reliance on a citizenship-by-investment programme to fund development.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roosevelt-skerrit.jpg" alt="Roosevelt Skerrit" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roosevelt Skerrit from Vieille Case, Dominica · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swearing_in_of_His_Excellency_Charles_A_Savarin,_DAH,_President_of_the_Commonwealth_of_Dominica_(31312241638).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
